WEBVTT

00:00:00.469 --> 00:00:05.165
Welcome to Alaventra. Rank in
search. Get recommended by AI.

00:00:06.164 --> 00:00:11.697
In tutorial 5.1, you'll read your Pipeline:
what runs this week, and what needs you.

00:00:12.707 --> 00:00:17.957
First, open Pipeline in the sidebar.
This badge shows the autopilot is on,

00:00:18.007 --> 00:00:20.326
and about how many
credits it uses a month.

00:00:21.266 --> 00:00:24.841
Pause stops every automatic
run until you resume.

00:00:24.891 --> 00:00:27.548
And What happens when walks
you through your whole week.

00:00:29.316 --> 00:00:33.406
Next, the blue card sums up your
week. Here, three things need you,

00:00:33.456 --> 00:00:35.233
and the rest runs on its own.

00:00:36.841 --> 00:00:40.891
Needs you lists each one with its own
button: start a suggested keyword,

00:00:40.941 --> 00:00:43.774
publish a written page,
or write the next one.

00:00:45.791 --> 00:00:49.776
Then look at This week. It lists
the next automatic runs in order,

00:00:49.826 --> 00:00:52.094
with the time and what each one works on.

00:00:53.791 --> 00:00:57.336
Back at the top, the card
names the next automatic run.

00:00:57.386 --> 00:01:02.821
Four figures show pages published, keywords
in the top 10, clicks from ladder pages,

00:01:02.871 --> 00:01:04.054
and credits used.

00:01:05.072 --> 00:01:09.422
And What happens next shows when Coming
up arrives, when your weekly run starts,

00:01:09.472 --> 00:01:10.771
and the monthly checks.

00:01:12.568 --> 00:01:15.533
Finally, open How a keyword ladder works.

00:01:15.583 --> 00:01:19.847
Six steps go from the plan to the main
keyword won, with your own numbers.

00:01:21.572 --> 00:01:25.997
Now you know where to look each week: what
needs you first, what runs on its own,

00:01:26.047 --> 00:01:27.719
and how your keywords climb.

00:01:29.093 --> 00:01:33.108
So: check the autopilot, handle
what needs you, look at this week,

00:01:33.158 --> 00:01:34.712
and read how a ladder works.

00:01:36.072 --> 00:01:41.555
Your week is on one screen. Next, start
a keyword ladder, in tutorial 5.2.
